* verify-basicfuncs.bp - does each SD BASIC intrinsic and operator return the
* RIGHT ANSWER?  PORT_ADOPTION queue 22, ranked item 5; the intent is the
* port's gplbld/basicfuncs.sb, written there 31 Aug 2026 for its 5.23 audit.
*
* THE QUESTION UNDER ALL THE OTHERS.  The verifiers beside this one ask whether
* a status was discarded, a lock stranded, a tier enforced.  This one asks
* whether the language answers correctly at all: every report, every VOC verb
* and every one of those other verifiers is built out of these functions, so a
* wrong answer here is an administrator being told something untrue at the
* deepest level there is.
*
* IT IS STAGED, COMPILED AND RUN BY verify-basicfuncs.py IN THE CALLER'S OWN
* ACCOUNT.  An ordinary program - NOT $internal - so it compiles and runs as an
* unprivileged user with no developer build.  Nothing here opens a file, a
* socket or the terminal, deliberately: see the NOT.TESTED block below.
*
* ***EVERY CASE PRINTS ONE LINE, ON ONE PATH, CARRYING BOTH THE ANSWER AND THE
* EXPECTATION:***
*
*     CASE|<name>|<got>|<want>|END
*
* ***THE "END" IS A TERMINATOR AND IT WAS PAID FOR ON THE FIRST RUN.***  Two
* of this file's cases - TRIMF and FMT.L - have an expectation that ENDS IN
* SPACES, and without a terminator the expectation is the last field on the
* line.  The first run, 12 Sep 2026, reported TRIMF as "expected 'ab', got
* 'ab  '": the Python half's own line.rstrip() had eaten the two spaces off
* its own input, and TRIMB passed in the same run because ITS spaces are
* LEADING.  The defect was in the instrument, not in SD.  With a terminator
* the trailing blanks are interior and nothing downstream can strip them
* without the line failing to parse, which is loud.
*
* ***THE COMPARISON IS DONE BY THE PYTHON HALF, NOT BY THE "if" BELOW, AND THAT
* IS THE ONE PLACE THIS FILE DELIBERATELY DIVERGES FROM THE PORT.***  The port
* prints OK| or FAIL| according to its own "if sg = sw", which makes the probe
* the judge of a language whose EQUALITY OPERATOR IS ONE OF THE THINGS UNDER
* TEST - a broken "=" would print OK for all 176 cases and the suite would go
* green.  Here the tally below is kept the same way and printed, but it is a
* SECOND instrument: Python re-derives the verdict from got and want, and a
* disagreement between the two counts is itself a reported row.
*
* AND IT REFUSES THE NULL CASE THREE WAYS.  PROBE.BEGIN and PROBE.DONE bracket
* the run, so a fault part way through cannot read as "no failures found";
* TALLY carries the case count, which Python reconciles against the number of
* CASE lines AND against the number of "gosub check" sites in this file, so a
* probe that stopped half way cannot score a clean pass.
*
* WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT TESTED, AND WHY.  The list is machine-readable:
* verify-basicfuncs.py reads these NOT.TESTED lines, reads the intrinsics table
* out of sdsys/GPL.BP/BCOMP, and FAILS if any intrinsic is neither exercised
* below nor named here.  So the coverage claim is measured, not asserted, and
* an intrinsic added to the compiler without a case or an exclusion turns this
* verifier red.
*
* NOT.TESTED: KEYIN KEYINC KEYINR KEYREADY INPUTBLK KEYCODE
*   - block on the terminal.
* NOT.TESTED: OPEN.SOCKET READ.SOCKET WRITE.SOCKET SOCKET.INFO
* NOT.TESTED: ACCEPT.SOCKET.CONNECTION CREATE.SERVER.SOCKET SERVER.ADDR
* NOT.TESTED: SET.SOCKET.MODE
*   - need a socket.
* NOT.TESTED: FILEINFO INDICES LISTINDEX SELECTINFO RECORDLOCKED TRANS RTRANS
* NOT.TESTED: XLATE ITYPE OBJECT OBJINFO SUBR CCALL OUTERJOIN
*   - need a file or a select list.  OUTERJOIN joins ACROSS FILES and its arity
*     is not satisfiable with literals: measured in the port 31 Aug 2026, the
*     literal form is a compile error rather than a value.
* NOT.TESTED: DATE TIME TIMEDATE SYSTEM STATUS ENV OS.ERROR SENTENCE ARG
* NOT.TESTED: ARG.COUNT COL1 COL2 GETREM INMAT RND
*   - session or host state: the answer is correct and different every run.
* NOT.TESTED: TERMINFO SAVE.SCREEN GETPU PRINTER.SETTING BINDKEY
* NOT.TESTED: GET.PORT.PARAMS SET.PORT.PARAMS GETNLS
*   - terminal or printer state.
* NOT.TESTED: CHGPHANT CONFIG UMASK CATALOGUED DIR GET.MESSAGES SYSMSG
* NOT.TESTED: SDENCRYPT SDDECRYPT
*   - change the process, or read something the process was started with.
*
* ***TWO NAMES CAME OFF THE PORT'S EXCLUSION LIST RATHER THAN ONTO THIS ONE,
* AND A THIRD PAIR WAS ON NEITHER LIST THERE.***  Measured 12 Sep 2026 against
* both trees' BCOMP, which carry the same 176 intrinsics:
*   DELETE  - the port both TESTS it (its DELETE.fn case) and names it excluded.
*             It is the dynamic-array DELETE() and it is tested below.
*   CHANGE  - the port files it under "change the process", beside CHGPHANT and
*             CONFIG.  It is nothing of the kind: gplsrc/op_chnge.c is a
*             substring replace, pure and satisfiable with literals.  Tested.
*   SWAP    - a synonym for CHANGE (BCOMP:581, both emit OP.CHANGE).  Named in
*             neither of the port's lists.  Tested.
*   ASSIGNED, UNASSIGNED - named in neither of the port's lists.  Tested.
* So the port's probe reaches 112 of its 176 intrinsics and accounts for 173 -
* 112 exercised plus 62 declared, less DELETE, which is on both lists.  This
* one reaches 116 and accounts for all 176.
*
* ***FILED WITH THE PORT 12 Sep 2026 AS `BUGS_FROM_LINUX_PORT.md` 8***, commit
* `8e8e7de` on `github.com/dmontaine/sd4windows`.  The count published there is
* 173; an earlier draft of this comment said 175, which was 176 less DELETE and
* forgot the three names that are on no list at all.
*
program zzbf

   cases = 0
   fails = 0

   crt 'PROBE.BEGIN'

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- arithmetic

   n = 'ABS' ; g = abs(-3)          ; w = 3          ; gosub check
   n = 'ABS.0' ; g = abs(0)         ; w = 0          ; gosub check
   n = 'INT' ; g = int(7.9)         ; w = 7          ; gosub check
   n = 'INT.neg' ; g = int(-7.9)    ; w = -7         ; gosub check
   n = 'MOD' ; g = mod(17, 5)       ; w = 2          ; gosub check
   n = 'MOD.neg' ; g = mod(-17, 5)  ; w = 3          ; gosub check
   n = 'REM' ; g = rem(17, 5)       ; w = 2          ; gosub check
   n = 'IDIV' ; g = idiv(17, 5)     ; w = 3          ; gosub check
   n = 'DIV' ; g = div(18, 3)       ; w = 6          ; gosub check
   n = 'RDIV' ; g = rdiv(17, 5)     ; w = 3          ; gosub check
   n = 'PWR' ; g = pwr(2, 10)       ; w = 1024       ; gosub check
   n = 'NEG' ; g = neg(5)           ; w = -5         ; gosub check
   n = 'MAX' ; g = max(3, 9)        ; w = 9          ; gosub check
   n = 'MIN' ; g = min(3, 9)        ; w = 3          ; gosub check
   n = 'SQRT' ; g = sqrt(16)        ; w = 4          ; gosub check
   n = 'NUM.yes' ; g = num('123')   ; w = 1          ; gosub check
   n = 'NUM.no' ; g = num('12a')    ; w = 0          ; gosub check
   n = 'ALPHA.yes' ; g = alpha('abc') ; w = 1        ; gosub check
   n = 'ALPHA.no' ; g = alpha('ab1') ; w = 0         ; gosub check

* ------------------------------------------------------------ transcendental
* SCALED TO INTEGERS, NOT FORMATTED WITH MD.  The port's first draft used
* oconv(x,'MDn') and every one of these "failed": MD does not round to n
* places, it INSERTS the point n digits from the right, so sin(30)=0.5 printed
* as 0.0001 and asin(0.5)=30 printed as 0.30.  The functions were right and the
* expectation was wrong - measured there 31 Aug 2026.  int(x*10000+0.5)
* compares the value itself and cannot be fooled that way.
* The angle functions take and return DEGREES, which these cases also pin.

   n = 'SIN' ; g = int(sin(30) * 10000 + 0.5)  ; w = 5000  ; gosub check
   n = 'COS' ; g = int(cos(60) * 10000 + 0.5)  ; w = 5000  ; gosub check
   n = 'TAN' ; g = int(tan(45) * 10000 + 0.5)  ; w = 10000 ; gosub check
   n = 'ASIN' ; g = int(asin(0.5) * 100 + 0.5) ; w = 3000  ; gosub check
   n = 'ACOS' ; g = int(acos(0.5) * 100 + 0.5) ; w = 6000  ; gosub check
   n = 'ATAN' ; g = int(atan(1) * 100 + 0.5)   ; w = 4500  ; gosub check
   n = 'EXP' ; g = int(exp(0) * 100 + 0.5)     ; w = 100   ; gosub check
   n = 'LN' ; g = int(ln(1) * 100 + 0.5)       ; w = 0     ; gosub check
   n = 'EXP.1' ; g = int(exp(1) * 1000 + 0.5)  ; w = 2718  ; gosub check

* ------------------------------------------------------------------- bitwise

   n = 'BITAND' ; g = bitand(12, 10)  ; w = 8    ; gosub check
   n = 'BITOR' ; g = bitor(12, 10)    ; w = 14   ; gosub check
   n = 'BITXOR' ; g = bitxor(12, 10)  ; w = 6    ; gosub check
   n = 'BITNOT' ; g = bitnot(0)       ; w = -1   ; gosub check
   n = 'BITSET' ; g = bitset(0, 3)    ; w = 8    ; gosub check
   n = 'BITRESET' ; g = bitreset(15, 3) ; w = 7  ; gosub check
   n = 'BITTEST.1' ; g = bittest(8, 3) ; w = 1   ; gosub check
   n = 'BITTEST.0' ; g = bittest(7, 3) ; w = 0   ; gosub check
* SHIFT's SIGN IS THE OPPOSITE WAY ROUND from the C operators: a POSITIVE count
* shifts RIGHT.  Measured in the port 31 Aug 2026 - shift(1,4) is 0, not 16.
* Pinned here in both directions so a change of convention cannot pass unseen.
   n = 'SHIFT.r' ; g = shift(16, 4)   ; w = 1    ; gosub check
   n = 'SHIFT.l' ; g = shift(1, -4)   ; w = 16   ; gosub check
* DTX RETURNS LOWER CASE, and that is Ladybridge's choice rather than a port
* artefact: op_misc.c's sprintf is "%x" and the upstream file is byte-identical.
* XTD accepts either case, so the round trip holds; pinned both ways.
   n = 'DTX' ; g = dtx(255)           ; w = 'ff' ; gosub check
   n = 'XTD.uc' ; g = xtd('FF')       ; w = 255  ; gosub check
   n = 'XTD.lc' ; g = xtd('ff')       ; w = 255  ; gosub check
   n = 'DTX.XTD.rt' ; g = xtd(dtx(48879)) ; w = 48879 ; gosub check

* -------------------------------------------------------------------- string

   n = 'LEN' ; g = len('hello')          ; w = 5        ; gosub check
   n = 'LEN.empty' ; g = len('')         ; w = 0        ; gosub check
   n = 'UPCASE' ; g = upcase('aBc')      ; w = 'ABC'    ; gosub check
   n = 'DOWNCASE' ; g = downcase('AbC')  ; w = 'abc'    ; gosub check
   n = 'SWAPCASE' ; g = swapcase('AbC')  ; w = 'aBc'    ; gosub check
   n = 'CHAR' ; g = char(65)             ; w = 'A'      ; gosub check
   n = 'SEQ' ; g = seq('A')              ; w = 65       ; gosub check
* ASCII() takes EBCDIC IN, so ascii(char(65)) is meaningless - 65 is ASCII 'A'
* but EBCDIC 65 is not.  EBCDIC 'A' is 0xC1 = 193, which is the real case.
   n = 'ASCII' ; g = ascii(char(193))    ; w = 'A'      ; gosub check
   n = 'EBCDIC' ; g = seq(ebcdic('A'))   ; w = 193      ; gosub check
   n = 'EBCDIC.rt' ; g = ascii(ebcdic('A')) ; w = 'A'   ; gosub check
   n = 'SPACE' ; g = len(space(7))       ; w = 7        ; gosub check
   n = 'STR' ; g = str('ab', 3)          ; w = 'ababab' ; gosub check
   n = 'TRIM' ; g = trim('  a  b  ')     ; w = 'a b'    ; gosub check
   n = 'TRIMF' ; g = trimf('  ab  ')     ; w = 'ab  '   ; gosub check
   n = 'TRIMB' ; g = trimb('  ab  ')     ; w = '  ab'   ; gosub check
   n = 'TRIM.char' ; g = trim('xxaxx', 'x') ; w = 'a'   ; gosub check
   n = 'INDEX.1' ; g = index('abcabc', 'b', 1) ; w = 2  ; gosub check
   n = 'INDEX.2' ; g = index('abcabc', 'b', 2) ; w = 5  ; gosub check
   n = 'INDEX.none' ; g = index('abc', 'z', 1) ; w = 0  ; gosub check
   n = 'COUNT' ; g = count('a,b,c', ',')  ; w = 2       ; gosub check
   n = 'DCOUNT' ; g = dcount('a,b,c', ',') ; w = 3      ; gosub check
   n = 'DCOUNT.empty' ; g = dcount('', ',') ; w = 0     ; gosub check
   n = 'FIELD' ; g = field('a,b,c', ',', 2) ; w = 'b'   ; gosub check
   n = 'FIELD.n' ; g = field('a,b,c,d', ',', 2, 2) ; w = 'b,c' ; gosub check
   n = 'FIELDSTORE' ; g = fieldstore('a,b,c', ',', 2, 1, 'X') ; w = 'a,X,c' ; gosub check
* SUBSTITUTE replaces whole ELEMENTS of a dynamic array, not substrings - so
* the operand has to carry marks or nothing matches.  CROP removes TRAILING
* empty elements, not internal ones; both pinned as measured 31 Aug 2026.
* SUBSTITUTE's FOURTH operand DOES NOT SPLIT THE SOURCE - three of the port's
* drafts assumed it did.  GPL.BP/_SUBST is the implementation and it settles
* it: the source is split by SYSTEM MARKS ("s = remove(str, delim)"), and the
* delimiter splits the OLD and NEW LISTS instead, through listindex() and
* field().  So a source with no marks is one element whatever delimiter is
* passed.  All three shapes are pinned: mark-split source with a list, a single
* old/new pair, and the no-marks case that legitimately changes nothing.
   n = 'SUBSTITUTE' ; g = substitute('a':@vm:'b':@vm:'c', 'a,c', 'X,Z', ',') ; w = 'X':@vm:'b':@vm:'Z' ; gosub check
   n = 'SUBSTITUTE.vm' ; g = substitute('a':@vm:'b':@vm:'a', 'a', 'Z', @vm) ; w = 'Z':@vm:'b':@vm:'Z' ; gosub check
   n = 'SUBSTITUTE.nomark' ; g = substitute('a,b,a', 'a', 'Z', ',') ; w = 'a,b,a' ; gosub check
   n = 'CROP.trailing' ; g = crop('a':@vm:'b':@vm) ; w = 'a':@vm:'b' ; gosub check
   n = 'CROP.internal' ; g = crop('a':@vm:@vm:'b') ; w = 'a':@vm:@vm:'b' ; gosub check
   n = 'QUOTE' ; g = quote('ab')         ; w = '"ab"'   ; gosub check
   n = 'DQUOTE' ; g = dquote('ab')       ; w = '"ab"'   ; gosub check
   n = 'SQUOTE' ; g = squote('ab')       ; w = "'ab'"   ; gosub check
   n = 'FOLD' ; g = fold('aaa bbb', 3)   ; w = 'aaa':@fm:'bbb' ; gosub check
   n = 'SOUNDEX' ; g = soundex('Robert') ; w = 'R163'   ; gosub check
   n = 'COMPARE.lt' ; g = compare('a', 'b') ; w = -1    ; gosub check
   n = 'COMPARE.eq' ; g = compare('a', 'a') ; w = 0     ; gosub check
   n = 'COMPARE.gt' ; g = compare('b', 'a') ; w = 1     ; gosub check
   n = 'CHECKSUM' ; g = (checksum('abc') = checksum('abc')) ; w = 1 ; gosub check
   n = 'CHECKSUM.diff' ; g = (checksum('abc') = checksum('abd')) ; w = 0 ; gosub check
* CONVERT()'s argument order is (from, to, string) - NOT (string, from, to).
* The port's first draft had it the other way and got 'XZ' back, which is the
* correct answer to the question it actually asked.  Measured 31 Aug 2026.
   n = 'CONVERT' ; g = convert('ac', 'XZ', 'abc') ; w = 'XbZ' ; gosub check
* CHANGE IS A SUBSTRING REPLACE AND SWAP IS ITS SYNONYM - BCOMP:581 and :451
* both emit OP.CHANGE.  The 4th argument is HOW MANY occurrences to change
* (default -1, all) and the 5th is WHICH occurrence to start at (default 1);
* gplsrc/op_chnge.c:95-105 is the order, and it is the reverse of the reading
* the names suggest.  Both optional arguments are pinned, in both positions,
* because a silent swap of the two would leave the 3-argument form correct.
   n = 'CHANGE' ; g = change('abcabc', 'b', 'Z') ; w = 'aZcaZc' ; gosub check
   n = 'CHANGE.count' ; g = change('abcabc', 'b', 'Z', 1) ; w = 'aZcabc' ; gosub check
   n = 'CHANGE.first' ; g = change('abcabc', 'b', 'Z', 1, 2) ; w = 'abcaZc' ; gosub check
   n = 'CHANGE.absent' ; g = change('abc', 'z', 'Z') ; w = 'abc' ; gosub check
   n = 'SWAP' ; g = swap('abcabc', 'b', 'Z') ; w = 'aZcaZc' ; gosub check
* CSVDQ SPLITS a CSV line into a dynamic array, it does not add quotes.
   n = 'CSVDQ' ; g = csvdq('a,b')        ; w = 'a':@fm:'b' ; gosub check
   n = 'CSVDQ.quoted' ; g = csvdq('"a,b",c') ; w = 'a,b':@fm:'c' ; gosub check
   n = 'MATCHFIELD' ; g = matchfield('abc123', '3A3N', 1) ; w = 'abc' ; gosub check

* ------------------------------------------------------------ dynamic arrays

   r = 'a':@vm:'b':@vm:'c'
   n = 'EXTRACT' ; g = extract(r, 1, 2, 0) ; w = 'b'    ; gosub check
   n = 'REPLACE' ; g = replace(r, 1, 2, 0, 'Z') ; w = 'a':@vm:'Z':@vm:'c' ; gosub check
   n = 'INSERT' ; g = insert(r, 1, 2, 0, 'Z') ; w = 'a':@vm:'Z':@vm:'b':@vm:'c' ; gosub check
   n = 'DELETE.fn' ; g = delete(r, 1, 2, 0) ; w = 'a':@vm:'c' ; gosub check
* LOCATE arr<1> SEARCHES FIELDS, NOT VALUES.  Two of the port's drafts fed it a
* value-marked string and got the ELSE branch, which was the right answer to
* the wrong question: with no @fm the whole string is field 1 and does not
* equal 'b'.  GPL.BP/ACOMP:707 is the codebase's own usage and it settles it -
* it builds its array with "ins x before label.names<1>", fields.  Both shapes
* are pinned below so the distinction cannot quietly change.  -1 marks "not
* found", so a miss can never be confused with a hit at position 0.
   rf = 'a':@fm:'b':@fm:'c'

   n = 'LOCATE.field'
   locate 'b' in rf<1> setting p then g = p else g = -1
   w = 2 ; gosub check

   n = 'LOCATE.field.first'
   locate 'a' in rf<1> setting p then g = p else g = -1
   w = 1 ; gosub check

   n = 'LOCATE.value'
   locate 'b' in r<1,1> setting p then g = p else g = -1
   w = 2 ; gosub check

   n = 'LOCATE.miss'
   locate 'z' in rf<1> setting p then g = p else g = -1
   w = -1 ; gosub check

   n = 'REUSE' ; g = reuse(1)            ; w = 1        ; gosub check
   n = 'SUM' ; g = sum(1:@vm:2:@vm:3)    ; w = 6        ; gosub check
   n = 'SUMMATION' ; g = summation(1:@vm:2:@vm:3) ; w = 6 ; gosub check
* VSLICE takes value N of every FIELD - a vertical slice down the fields, which
* needs @fm in the operand.  The port's first draft fed it a single field and
* got that field's value 1 back, which was the right answer to the wrong
* question.
   n = 'VSLICE' ; g = vslice('a':@vm:'b':@fm:'c':@vm:'d', 1) ; w = 'a':@fm:'c' ; gosub check
   n = 'VSLICE.2' ; g = vslice('a':@vm:'b':@fm:'c':@vm:'d', 2) ; w = 'b':@fm:'d' ; gosub check
   n = 'SPLICE' ; g = splice('a':@vm:'b', '-', 'x':@vm:'y') ; w = 'a-x':@vm:'b-y' ; gosub check
   n = 'REMOVE' ; s = 'a':@vm:'b' ; g = remove(s, d) ; w = 'a' ; gosub check

* ------------------------------------------------ the S-suffix (vector) forms

   n = 'ABSS' ; g = abss(-1:@vm:-2)      ; w = 1:@vm:2  ; gosub check
   n = 'NEGS' ; g = negs(1:@vm:2)        ; w = -1:@vm:-2 ; gosub check
   n = 'LENS' ; g = lens('a':@vm:'bb')   ; w = 1:@vm:2   ; gosub check
   n = 'NUMS' ; g = nums('1':@vm:'x')    ; w = 1:@vm:0   ; gosub check
   n = 'CATS' ; g = cats('a':@vm:'b', 'X':@vm:'Y') ; w = 'aX':@vm:'bY' ; gosub check
   n = 'COUNTS' ; g = counts('aa':@vm:'aaa', 'a') ; w = 2:@vm:3 ; gosub check
   n = 'EQS' ; g = eqs(1:@vm:2, 1:@vm:9) ; w = 1:@vm:0   ; gosub check
   n = 'NES' ; g = nes(1:@vm:2, 1:@vm:9) ; w = 0:@vm:1   ; gosub check
   n = 'GTS' ; g = gts(2:@vm:1, 1:@vm:2) ; w = 1:@vm:0   ; gosub check
   n = 'LTS' ; g = lts(1:@vm:2, 2:@vm:1) ; w = 1:@vm:0   ; gosub check
   n = 'GES' ; g = ges(1:@vm:2, 1:@vm:3) ; w = 1:@vm:0   ; gosub check
   n = 'LES' ; g = les(1:@vm:3, 1:@vm:2) ; w = 1:@vm:0   ; gosub check
   n = 'ANDS' ; g = ands(1:@vm:0, 1:@vm:1) ; w = 1:@vm:0 ; gosub check
   n = 'ORS' ; g = ors(1:@vm:0, 0:@vm:0) ; w = 1:@vm:0   ; gosub check
   n = 'NOTS' ; g = nots(1:@vm:0)        ; w = 0:@vm:1   ; gosub check
   n = 'MODS' ; g = mods(17:@vm:18, 5:@vm:5) ; w = 2:@vm:3 ; gosub check
   n = 'IFS' ; g = ifs(1:@vm:0, 'y':@vm:'y', 'n':@vm:'n') ; w = 'y':@vm:'n' ; gosub check
   n = 'STRS' ; g = strs('a':@vm:'b', 2) ; w = 'aa':@vm:'bb' ; gosub check
   n = 'TRIMS' ; g = trims(' a ':@vm:' b ') ; w = 'a':@vm:'b' ; gosub check
   n = 'TRIMFS' ; g = trimfs(' a':@vm:' b') ; w = 'a':@vm:'b' ; gosub check
   n = 'TRIMBS' ; g = trimbs('a ':@vm:'b ') ; w = 'a':@vm:'b' ; gosub check
   n = 'FOLDS' ; g = folds('aaa bbb':@vm:'cc', 3) ; w = 'aaa':@fm:'bbb':@vm:'cc' ; gosub check
   n = 'SOUNDEXS' ; g = soundexs('Robert':@vm:'Rupert') ; w = 'R163':@vm:'R163' ; gosub check
   n = 'INDEXS' ; g = indexs('abc':@vm:'xbz', 'b', 1) ; w = 2:@vm:2 ; gosub check
   n = 'FIELDS' ; g = fields('a,b':@vm:'c,d', ',', 2) ; w = 'b':@vm:'d' ; gosub check
   n = 'SUBSTRINGS' ; g = substrings('abcd':@vm:'efgh', 2, 2) ; w = 'bc':@vm:'fg' ; gosub check
   n = 'MAXIMUM' ; g = maximum(3:@vm:9:@vm:5) ; w = 9   ; gosub check
   n = 'MINIMUM' ; g = minimum(3:@vm:9:@vm:5) ; w = 3   ; gosub check
   n = 'SPACES' ; g = lens(spaces(2:@vm:3)) ; w = 2:@vm:3 ; gosub check
* RAISE promotes a mark one level UP (@vm to @fm); LOWER demotes it.  The
* port's first draft had RAISE the wrong way round.
   n = 'RAISE' ; g = raise('a':@vm:'b') ; w = 'a':@fm:'b' ; gosub check
   n = 'LOWER' ; g = lower('a':@vm:'b') ; w = 'a':@sm:'b' ; gosub check
   n = 'RAISE.LOWER.rt' ; g = lower(raise('a':@vm:'b')) ; w = 'a':@vm:'b' ; gosub check

* --------------------------------------------------------------- conversions

   n = 'OCONV.MD2' ; g = oconv(1234, 'MD2')   ; w = '12.34'  ; gosub check
   n = 'ICONV.MD2' ; g = iconv('12.34', 'MD2') ; w = 1234    ; gosub check
   n = 'OCONV.MCU' ; g = oconv('abc', 'MCU')  ; w = 'ABC'    ; gosub check
   n = 'OCONV.MCL' ; g = oconv('ABC', 'MCL')  ; w = 'abc'    ; gosub check
   n = 'ICONV.D.rt' ; g = oconv(iconv('01 JAN 2000', 'D'), 'D-YMD[4,2,2]') ; w = '2000-01-01' ; gosub check
* MTH's am/pm CASE IS AN OPTION, not a constant: op_oconv.c picks "AM"/"PM"
* when OptAMPMUpcase is set and "am"/"pm" otherwise, and lower case is the
* default.  Identical upstream.  Pinned as the default so a change of default
* shows up here rather than in somebody's report.
   n = 'ICONV.MT.rt' ; g = oconv(iconv('12:30', 'MT'), 'MTH') ; w = '12:30pm' ; gosub check
   n = 'ICONV.MT.val' ; g = iconv('12:30', 'MT') ; w = 45000 ; gosub check
   n = 'OCONVS' ; g = oconvs(1234:@vm:5678, 'MD2') ; w = '12.34':@vm:'56.78' ; gosub check
   n = 'ICONVS' ; g = iconvs('12.34':@vm:'56.78', 'MD2') ; w = 1234:@vm:5678 ; gosub check
   n = 'FMT.R' ; g = fmt('7', 'R%3')          ; w = '007'    ; gosub check
   n = 'FMT.L' ; g = fmt('ab', 'L#4')         ; w = 'ab  '   ; gosub check
   n = 'FMTS' ; g = fmts('7':@vm:'8', 'R%3')  ; w = '007':@vm:'008' ; gosub check

* ----------------------------------------- VARTYPE, ASSIGNED and UNASSIGNED
* VARTYPE RETURNS THE DESCRIPTOR TYPE CODE, and the codes are gplsrc/descr.h
* :221-230 - UNASSIGNED 0, INTEGER 2, FLOATNUM 3, STRING 5.  The port asserted
* only "vartype(1) is not empty", which passes for any of them; these pin the
* value, so a descriptor type renumbered in descr.h without its dependants
* being swept shows up here.
*
* ***ZZ.UNSET IS NEVER ASSIGNED ANYWHERE IN THIS FILE AND THAT IS THE POINT.***
* It makes BCOMP print the warning "ZZ.UNSET is not assigned a value"
* (message 2825, BCOMP:1497), which is a WARNING and not an error - warnings
* count towards the error total only under the compiler's warnings-as-errors
* option (BCOMP:13072), which is off.  verify-basicfuncs.py asserts that the
* warning appears EXACTLY ONCE: it is the null-case guard for these three
* cases, because a ZZ.UNSET that had somehow acquired a value would make
* unassigned() and vartype() answer correctly about the wrong thing.

   vi = 1
   vs = 'a'
   n = 'VARTYPE.int' ; g = vartype(vi)      ; w = 2  ; gosub check
   n = 'VARTYPE.str' ; g = vartype(vs)      ; w = 5  ; gosub check
   n = 'VARTYPE.unset' ; g = vartype(zz.unset) ; w = 0 ; gosub check
   n = 'ASSIGNED.yes' ; g = assigned(vi)    ; w = 1  ; gosub check
   n = 'ASSIGNED.no' ; g = assigned(zz.unset) ; w = 0 ; gosub check
   n = 'UNASSIGNED.yes' ; g = unassigned(zz.unset) ; w = 1 ; gosub check
   n = 'UNASSIGNED.no' ; g = unassigned(vi) ; w = 0  ; gosub check

* ------------------------------------------------------------------ operators

   n = 'OP.add' ; g = 2 + 3            ; w = 5          ; gosub check
   n = 'OP.sub' ; g = 7 - 2            ; w = 5          ; gosub check
   n = 'OP.mul' ; g = 6 * 7            ; w = 42         ; gosub check
   n = 'OP.div' ; g = 20 / 4           ; w = 5          ; gosub check
   n = 'OP.cat' ; g = 'a' : 'b'        ; w = 'ab'       ; gosub check
   n = 'OP.prec' ; g = 2 + 3 * 4       ; w = 14         ; gosub check
   n = 'OP.paren' ; g = (2 + 3) * 4    ; w = 20         ; gosub check
   n = 'OP.eq' ; g = (1 = 1)           ; w = 1          ; gosub check
   n = 'OP.ne' ; g = (1 # 2)           ; w = 1          ; gosub check
   n = 'OP.lt' ; g = (1 < 2)           ; w = 1          ; gosub check
   n = 'OP.gt' ; g = (2 > 1)           ; w = 1          ; gosub check
   n = 'OP.le' ; g = (2 <= 2)          ; w = 1          ; gosub check
   n = 'OP.ge' ; g = (2 >= 2)          ; w = 1          ; gosub check
   n = 'OP.and' ; g = (1 and 0)        ; w = 0          ; gosub check
   n = 'OP.or' ; g = (1 or 0)          ; w = 1          ; gosub check
   n = 'OP.not' ; g = not(0)           ; w = 1          ; gosub check
   n = 'OP.matches' ; g = ('abc' matches '3A') ; w = 1  ; gosub check
   n = 'OP.matches.no' ; g = ('ab1' matches '3A') ; w = 0 ; gosub check
   n = 'OP.strcmp' ; g = ('a' < 'b')   ; w = 1          ; gosub check
   n = 'OP.numstr' ; g = ('10' > '9')  ; w = 1          ; gosub check
   n = 'OP.uminus' ; g = -(3)          ; w = -3         ; gosub check
   n = 'OP.fmt.dyn' ; g = 'a':@fm:'b'<1,1> ; w = 'a':@fm:'b' ; gosub check

* ------------------------------------------------------------------- summary

   crt 'TALLY|' : cases : '|' : fails
   crt 'PROBE.DONE'
   stop

* ======================================================================
* check - print one case.  ONE LINE, ONE PATH.
*
* The marks are converted to visible letters IN PLACE rather than through a
* helper function: CONVERT is one-for-one, so F, V and S each stand for exactly
* one mark and a mark-versus-space difference stays readable in the transcript
* instead of being invisible.
*
* The values are compared as STRINGS deliberately - a numeric compare would
* call 0 and '0.0' equal and hide a formatting regression.  The "if" keeps this
* probe's OWN tally, which the Python half reconciles against the verdict it
* derives itself; it does NOT decide the verdict.

check:
   cases += 1
   sg = g : ''
   sw = w : ''
   convert @fm to 'F' in sg
   convert @vm to 'V' in sg
   convert @sm to 'S' in sg
   convert @fm to 'F' in sw
   convert @vm to 'V' in sw
   convert @sm to 'S' in sw
   if sg # sw then fails += 1
   crt 'CASE|' : n : '|' : sg : '|' : sw : '|END'
   return

end
